<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Implementation Details for Baselines</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The hyperparameter settings for the baselines in our experiments are as follows:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VCD</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Leng et al. 2024</a>)</cite>: We add 500 steps of Gaussian noise to the original image to construct the contrastive visual input, and the hyperparameters for contrastive decoding are set to <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PAI</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu, Zheng, and Chen 2024</a>)</cite>: We activate the PAI method starting from layer 2 (counting from 0), with hyperparameters set to <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1.1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VAR</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kang et al. 2025</a>)</cite>: The hyperparameters in this method are set as follows: <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=20</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.6</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AD-HH</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. 2025</a>)</cite>: We set the hallucination threshold <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> for attention heads to 0.5. For the definition of hallucination heads, please refer to the original paper.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VAF</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yin, Si, and Wang 2025a</a>)</cite>: We set <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.15</annotation></semantics></math>, and activate this method from layer 9 to layer 14 (counting from 0).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TARAC</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al. 2025</a>)</cite>: We set <math id="A1.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, and activate this method from layer 9 to layer 15 (counting from 0).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Note: Parameters with the same name may have different meanings across methods; please refer to the original papers for their specific definitions.</span></p>
</div>
